/target
**/*.rs.bk

# Compiled artifacts must never be committed. cria carries a 206 KB .rlib in its
# history; that is the mistake this line exists to prevent.
*.rlib
*.rmeta
*.so
*.dylib

# Secrets. Deploy env files live on the host at /opt/stacks/, never in the repo.
*.env
!.env.example
/deploy/*.secret

# Local state
/spec/*.tmp.json
.direnv/

# Personal Claude Code config for this checkout: plugin choices, extra permissions.
# `.claude/settings.json` is the project's own -- the rust-check hook and the cargo
# permissions everyone needs -- and belongs in the repo. This one does not, and was
# ignored only by never being added until a `git add -A` swept it into a commit.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Generated at release time by `cargo about`; never committed.
THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md

# Scratch analyses under md/. Not documentation -- tool output kept for reference,
# and it may contain credentials. These were ignored only by never being added,
# which a single `git add -A` would undo.
/md/bloat-detector/
/md/minify/
/md/ruflo-audit/

# Python bytecode from the helper scripts under test-scripts/. A .pyc was tracked until
# 2026-09-06; it embeds the absolute path it was compiled from and is regenerated anyway.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Internal working material. These stay on disk and out of the published repository:
# implementation plans and session handoffs are execution scaffolding rather than
# documentation, the manual-check procedures name hosts on a private tailnet, and the
# deploy kit and live-test runners target one specific dev instance and are unusable by
# anyone else. The design documents under md/ are deliberately still tracked -- they are
# the "why" a contributor needs.
/deploy/
/test-scripts/
/run-live-tests-token.sh
/run-live-tests-password.sh
/md/*-plan.md
/md/*-handoff.md
/md/2026-09-06-release-binaries-design.md
/md/MANUAL-CHECKS.md
/md/MANUAL-CHECKS2.md
/md/MANUAL-CHECKS-BUGS.md
/md/overview.md

# Rendered demo media. The tape script is tracked and regenerates these; the output is
# multi-megabyte binary that would sit in history forever.
/docs/demo/*.gif
/docs/demo/*.mp4
/docs/demo/*.webm
/docs/demo/*-agent.gif
# ...except the one the README embeds. Committed deliberately and knowingly: a GIF in
# git history cannot be removed later without rewriting it, and a README image hosted
# anywhere else breaks the day that host or release is deleted.
!/docs/demo/tui-do-agent.gif
